course: dictionary
lesson: 10472
title: Tummy and body words
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: A tummy is your stomach or belly. It is a friendly, everyday word, and people often use it when they talk to children. Context tells you which meaning fits, so read the words around it. «She had a tummy ache after eating too many sweets.» The sweets are the clue: the ache is a pain in her belly.
explain: Tummy is also used in phrases that are not about the belly itself. «Butterflies in my tummy» means you feel nervous, as if something is fluttering inside you before a test or a show. Try your meaning in the sentence: does «I feel nervous before the show» make sense in place of the phrase? If it does, you have understood it.
explain: In science lessons, the correct word for the organ that digests food is stomach. Tummy often means the whole belly, so the two words are close but not the same. Choosing the right word for the right place is a sign of a careful writer.
fact: A tummy is your stomach or belly.
fact: «Tummy ache» means a pain in your belly.
fact: «Butterflies in my tummy» means you feel nervous.
fact: A tummy rumble is a sound made by gas and liquid moving along your gut.
fact: In science, stomach is the proper word for the organ that digests food.
exercise: «She had a tummy ache after eating too many sweets.» What is a tummy ache? | A pain in your toes | A cold in your nose | *A pain in your belly | A feeling of being sleepy
exercise: «I had butterflies in my tummy before the show.» What does this phrase tell you? | I felt sleepy after lunch | I felt very hungry | *I felt nervous | I felt cold and wet
exercise: A tummy rumble is gas and liquid moving along your gut. What is a tummy rumble? | A bug that makes you sick | A sore spot where you bumped your knee | A type of football move | *A sound made by gas and liquid moving in your gut
test: In science, what is the proper word for the organ that digests food? | *stomach | tummy | elbow | belly button
test: «Loving a food does not make it healthy» is followed by a rabbit with tummy trouble. What does tummy trouble mean? | A broken tooth only | Running very fast | Trouble with its ears | *Problems in the belly
exam: In the seat belt sentence, where should the belt go? | Round your neck | On your ankles | Across your tummy only | *Across your chest and hips, not your tummy or neck
